From c5488923c7142046ffb3a37e00149460d97b5a33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shahed <jamshidalinezhadian@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 21:17:06 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] wifi: undef NAN before the HIDL headers in service.cpp

The HIDL wifi enums IfaceType and RttPeerType have a member named NAN
(Neighbour Awareness Networking), while bionic math.h defines NAN as
__builtin_nanf(""). On Android 13 one of the system headers included by
service.cpp pulls in math.h, so every IfaceType::NAN in the generated
types.h expanded to a function call, giving 12 errors.

Same fix and placement as the sibling files wifi_iface_util.cpp and
wifi_feature_flags.cpp, and as AOSP's own wifi VTS tests.

Change-Id: Id4400eae80374e34c5e6aafce5b5e8f54f19833b
---
 wifi/1.0-legacy/service.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/wifi/1.0-legacy/service.cpp b/wifi/1.0-legacy/service.cpp
index 3f7f609..93b0664 100644
--- a/wifi/1.0-legacy/service.cpp
+++ b/wifi/1.0-legacy/service.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <utils/Looper.h>
 #include <utils/StrongPointer.h>
 
+#undef NAN  // NAN is defined in bionic/libc/include/math.h
 #include "wifi.h"
 #include "wifi_feature_flags.h"
 #include "wifi_legacy_hal.h"
